WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:14.818
Derivative of the inverse
Let f of x be x cubed plus x. We want the derivative of the inverse at two,
without finding an explicit formula for that inverse.

2
00:00:14.818 --> 00:00:31.455
Justify the bijection
The derivative of f is three x squared plus one, which is always positive.
Together with continuity and the limits at infinity, this establishes a
bijection on the real numbers.

3
00:00:31.455 --> 00:00:44.000
Find the correct preimage
Find the preimage of two. Try one. One cubed plus one equals two, so the
inverse evaluated at two is one.

4
00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:57.455
Check the denominator
Calculate the derivative at one to obtain four, which is nonzero. We can now
apply the inverse derivative formula by taking the reciprocal.

5
00:00:57.455 --> 00:01:13.182
Conclude
The inverse's derivative at two is one divided by the original derivative at
one, or one quarter. Evaluate the original derivative at the preimage, not at
the output.
